AI Assistant - Welcome Center
1. Feature Core Intent & Value Proposition
Feature Name: CSP Welcome Center AI Assistant (In-Portal Support Copilot)

Target Users: All new Palo Alto Networks Customer Support Portal (CSP) users (including migrated CyberArk/Idira accounts).

Primary Objective: Enable newly onboarded customers to ask administrative questions in their native language, receiving instant, conversational responses backed directly by verified Knowledge Base (KB) articles, Onboarding FAQs, and documentation.

Core KPI: Self-service enablement, immediate time-to-answer for new users, and admin case deflection.

2. Technical Scope & Data Sources
Knowledge Ingestion Base:

Official Palo Alto Networks Knowledge Base (KB) articles.

CSP Onboarding Walkthrough Guides & FAQ documentation.

System operational status and known portal sync behavior (e.g., 24–48 hour case access sync window).

Key Functional Capabilities:

Multilingual Input & Output: Natural language processing allowing users to query in any language and receive answers in that same language.

Direct Source Citation: Every generated answer must cite and link to the source KB article(s) or FAQ page.


3. Eamples to User Queries (Training & Prompt Scenarios)

User Query: "Why can't I see my support cases right now?" / "I just logged in, where are my cases?"

Expected AI Response: Explain the standard 24–48 hour system sync window for new/provisioned accounts, reassure the user their profile is active, and link to KB Article: How to Access Support Cases After CSP Provisioning.

Account & Role Management:

User Query: "How do I add a new user to the account?"

Expected AI Response: Outline Super User steps (Members ➔ Manage Users), explain role types (Super User vs. Standard), and note activation link requirements.

Asset Discovery & License Management:

User Query: "Where are my migrated Idira entitlements?"

Expected AI Response: Direct user to Products ➔ Assets and highlight the Idira tab or Account Selector.

Migration & Vault Analysis Tool (VAT):

User Query: "How do I submit my VAT .VHC file for migration?"

Expected AI Response: Detail the steps to download from Idira Marketplace, run the assessment, create an Admin Case under Upgrades and Extensions, and upload the encrypted .VHC file.

4. Design & Guardrail Guidelines for Cursor
Response Tone: Clear, concise, helpful, and professional. Avoid fluffy intro phrases or robotic meta-announcements.

Citation Rule: Always require explicit Markdown link references to source articles in generated responses.

Safety & Escalation Guardrail: If an issue relates to a critical production outage (S1 Critical) or unresolvable technical bug, immediately instruct the user to navigate to Create a Case ➔ Technical Case.